WEBVTT

00:03.460 --> 00:07.110
And now, let's read a fax
message from our audience.

00:07.570 --> 00:09.460
"I love Claskey Klasky.

00:09.460 --> 00:12.730
I hear rumors about you two breaking up,

00:12.730 --> 00:14.880
but you're actually on
really good terms, right?"

00:14.880 --> 00:17.450
From I Believe in You,
Claskey Klasky of Saitama.

00:17.450 --> 00:19.090
Do they really believe in us?

00:19.090 --> 00:21.100
Would they ask us that if
they really believed in us?

00:21.100 --> 00:24.210
W-Well, so are you two
not getting along, then?

00:24.440 --> 00:25.620
Of course we are.

00:25.620 --> 00:27.310
We're super close.

00:27.310 --> 00:30.600
We were talking so much in the car,
our manager got angry at us.

00:30.600 --> 00:32.310
Tchaiko-chan, what's wrong?

00:32.310 --> 00:33.560
I have bed hair.

00:33.560 --> 00:37.550
I totally fell asleep in the car
on the way here, like this.

00:37.820 --> 00:40.310
Quit contradicting me!

00:40.310 --> 00:42.060
That kick hurt, damn it.

00:43.040 --> 00:45.060
Are you watching, Saitaman?

00:45.060 --> 00:48.170
You shouldn't say you believe
in someone when you don't.

00:48.170 --> 00:51.110
Bąda-chan and I don't believe
in each other at all<i>.</i>

00:51.110 --> 00:54.360
Please Stand By

01:15.530 --> 01:16.460
What is this place?

01:16.460 --> 01:18.010
Hello.

01:21.220 --> 01:22.940
Tesoluto.

01:22.940 --> 01:24.480
Absatz.

01:25.340 --> 01:26.310
Fine.

01:30.600 --> 01:31.570
So?

01:31.570 --> 01:34.380
"You don't have to come
to the agency anymore."

01:34.380 --> 01:36.900
Oh, you were fired?

01:39.480 --> 01:40.460
Wh...

01:40.660 --> 01:42.370
Wh...

01:42.570 --> 01:46.960
Why?!

03:43.810 --> 03:44.910
Why?!

03:45.050 --> 03:46.520
Why?!

03:46.520 --> 03:48.780
You know damn well why he ditched you.

03:48.780 --> 03:50.850
It's because of what you
said at the talk show.

03:50.850 --> 03:52.210
Claskey Klasky's over.

03:52.210 --> 03:53.920
I'm making my solo debut next.

03:54.150 --> 03:57.000
What? He kicked you out, too.

03:54.790 --> 04:00.210
19: "Love, And You Shall Die"

03:57.000 --> 03:58.170
You're right here!

03:58.170 --> 03:59.050
Here?

03:59.050 --> 04:00.750
Where even are we?!

04:01.810 --> 04:02.870
Um...

04:02.870 --> 04:03.590
What?!

04:04.080 --> 04:05.220
Welcome.

04:06.110 --> 04:06.890
What?

04:07.540 --> 04:08.680
This is your place?

04:08.680 --> 04:09.670
Yup.

04:09.670 --> 04:11.310
It's the Otowakan main hall.

04:11.660 --> 04:16.440
I thought everyone was in
their own rooms and stuff.

04:23.070 --> 04:25.210
People of the mansion,

04:25.210 --> 04:29.540
welcome to the world of
the Musik "Swan Lake."

04:29.820 --> 04:32.220
Swan Lake...

04:32.220 --> 04:34.080
This is my Musik?

04:34.080 --> 04:35.080
Look over there.

04:38.370 --> 04:39.350
An eye?!

04:39.350 --> 04:42.800
I am the evil sorcerer bird, Rothbart.

04:43.140 --> 04:44.420
Hasshie, that's you, right?

04:44.420 --> 04:45.210
No way.

04:45.210 --> 04:45.930
He's way too huge.

04:46.180 --> 04:49.470
I am the demon bird, Rothbart.

04:49.960 --> 04:51.060
Hasshie.

04:51.060 --> 04:52.860
Rothbart.

04:52.860 --> 04:53.680
Okay?

04:54.080 --> 04:57.570
This mansion will soon become
the stage of a tragedy.

04:57.570 --> 04:58.950
Why is that?

04:59.130 --> 05:00.480
Why is it?

05:01.190 --> 05:03.730
Those who fall in love inside the mansion

05:03.730 --> 05:07.110
will be captured by the cursed black bird,

05:08.070 --> 05:09.990
and meet certain doom.

05:10.260 --> 05:11.320
What the hell?

05:11.320 --> 05:13.600
What's the point of this crazy Musik?

05:13.600 --> 05:15.670
It probably has to do with
the shock of rejection.

05:15.670 --> 05:16.570
Stop it!

05:16.570 --> 05:17.910
Stop dragging me into this!

05:17.910 --> 05:20.340
How am I supposed to stop
what I'm not doing on purpose?!

05:20.860 --> 05:24.410
Fall in love in the mansion,
and it's game over.

05:24.410 --> 05:26.800
Fall in love, though? Now?
That's not going to happen.

05:26.800 --> 05:28.180
Indeed.

05:28.180 --> 05:31.320
There is no such sinfulness here.

05:31.320 --> 05:33.810
Senpai's absolutely right, Rothenmeier.

05:34.000 --> 05:35.830
It's Rothbart.

05:36.220 --> 05:41.460
The chances of falling in love in this mansion
are 70 percent higher than elsewhere.

05:41.460 --> 05:42.710
Beware.

05:43.410 --> 05:44.650
Hard mode!

05:44.650 --> 05:45.520
You're terrible!

05:45.520 --> 05:48.570
How could you set fire to our hearts
and then forbid us from falling in love?

05:48.570 --> 05:52.220
Isn't forbidden love more enticing
than the normal kind?

05:52.220 --> 05:53.540
I know, right?

05:54.370 --> 05:58.240
I've been meaning to ask...
Who are those people?

05:58.240 --> 06:00.720
Motes' fans from school.

06:00.720 --> 06:02.770
They kind of invited themselves over.

06:02.770 --> 06:05.290
Don't allow such wicked
creatures into my mansion.

06:05.290 --> 06:06.800
<i>Whose</i> mansion?

06:07.060 --> 06:08.210
Motes-sama...

06:08.210 --> 06:10.060
Shall we fall in love?

06:10.060 --> 06:11.930
Right now?

06:12.220 --> 06:13.860
Nice, nice!

06:13.860 --> 06:15.770
My naughty good girls!

06:20.980 --> 06:22.820
Don't do it!

06:29.320 --> 06:30.280
Motes!

06:30.280 --> 06:31.120
Oh, no!

06:38.340 --> 06:40.300
A couple is born.

06:40.300 --> 06:42.170
But that was three-to-one.

06:42.170 --> 06:44.210
Love takes many forms.

06:44.550 --> 06:48.900
Pair off, and the cursed black
birds consume you, you say?

06:48.900 --> 06:50.220
They weren't black, though.

06:50.470 --> 06:52.100
Could that have been Hasshie?

06:52.100 --> 06:53.710
It's Hasshie, obviously.

06:53.710 --> 06:56.540
To think he was eaten by
birds for his depravity...

06:56.990 --> 06:58.850
A fitting end to Wolf's life.

06:58.850 --> 07:01.980
This is the power of Musik...

07:02.760 --> 07:09.690
This mansion is cursed with the Musik
of love and death, "Swan Lake"!

07:11.370 --> 07:12.880
Of love and death?

07:12.880 --> 07:14.180
Musik?

07:14.180 --> 07:16.120
That is correct.

07:16.320 --> 07:18.820
Be imprisoned here forever,

07:18.820 --> 07:21.720
or fall in love and fall prey to my talons.

07:21.720 --> 07:23.550
Make your choice.

07:23.550 --> 07:26.760
Bam, you got served.

07:27.680 --> 07:30.340
Wh-What terrifying Musik!

07:30.340 --> 07:31.880
She's totally bragging.

07:32.050 --> 07:35.500
Th-Th-This calls for...

07:36.910 --> 07:40.520
Okay, everyone, I have curry!

07:40.520 --> 07:42.970
My little kitten,
when did you get that ready?

07:42.970 --> 07:43.980
Stay back!

07:48.060 --> 07:50.650
There's plenty for everyone!

07:51.730 --> 07:53.960
Cut it out!

07:56.550 --> 08:01.500
A-A-All this stuff's going to make
everyone fall in love with you!

08:01.500 --> 08:02.710
What stuff?

08:03.330 --> 08:03.960
Food.

08:04.600 --> 08:05.420
Maid outfit.

08:05.990 --> 08:07.250
Your smile.

08:07.490 --> 08:09.310
Look at their faces!

08:10.060 --> 08:11.760
Food...

08:12.870 --> 08:15.570
But I'm always like this.

08:15.570 --> 08:16.640
Yeesh...

08:16.970 --> 08:18.090
Food.

08:18.090 --> 08:19.060
Lunch.

08:19.060 --> 08:20.190
It smells good.

08:20.190 --> 08:21.420
Open your eyes.

08:21.420 --> 08:23.070
It's the Musik's curse.

08:23.070 --> 08:24.830
It's a temptation of love and death!

08:24.830 --> 08:26.290
It's not such a big deal.

08:26.290 --> 08:27.390
Yes, it is.

08:27.390 --> 08:28.610
Don't fall for it.

08:28.610 --> 08:31.030
Don't fall for the Musik's curse!

08:28.730 --> 08:29.570
Food...

08:29.570 --> 08:30.270
Food...

08:30.270 --> 08:31.030
Food...

08:31.030 --> 08:32.110
Oh, all right.

08:34.820 --> 08:36.640
Look over here.

08:36.640 --> 08:39.240
You should fall in love with me,
not with my little kitten.

08:39.240 --> 08:42.010
Liszt-san, you're trying to protect me.

08:42.010 --> 08:44.240
Don't you dare fall for me.

08:44.240 --> 08:45.960
I'll be okay.

08:46.220 --> 08:48.370
Now, look at me.

08:51.600 --> 08:54.270
You guys seriously suck.

08:57.410 --> 08:58.280
My.

09:01.710 --> 09:03.480
S-Sorry.

09:03.480 --> 09:05.010
It's all right.

09:05.010 --> 09:07.220
You have an eye for true beauty.

09:16.280 --> 09:17.700
No way.

09:18.620 --> 09:20.710
I warned you.

09:20.710 --> 09:22.330
A couple is born.

09:22.560 --> 09:24.390
B-Because they locked eyes?

09:24.390 --> 09:26.990
They just had a brief moment.

09:26.990 --> 09:29.420
An expression of youthful
libido leads to tragedy.

09:29.620 --> 09:32.440
B-Blame not a passionate infatuation.

09:32.440 --> 09:36.150
Though his cheeks may glow a forbidden
red, it is but a fleeting fancy...

09:36.150 --> 09:39.180
True fire cannot be found in false games.

09:39.450 --> 09:41.270
It's your fault, Tchaiko-chan.

09:41.270 --> 09:45.050
You didn't even do good work, and now
you're causing trouble with your Musik.

09:45.970 --> 09:51.110
I think I know why that man
didn't need you anymore.

09:51.570 --> 09:52.940
You wanna go?

09:56.180 --> 09:59.350
Hasshie is probably satisfied
with his prey right now.

10:00.830 --> 10:01.780
Cho-chan-san!

10:01.780 --> 10:02.830
You can't go out now!

10:02.830 --> 10:04.120
I have to go.

10:04.120 --> 10:06.160
I'm going to lose all my items.

10:06.390 --> 10:07.810
Is he talking about his game?

10:07.810 --> 10:09.980
He values his game more than his life.

10:09.980 --> 10:10.720
This is bad.

10:10.720 --> 10:12.000
The hallway's not safe.

10:12.000 --> 10:13.850
We have to bring him back right away.

10:15.020 --> 10:16.070
Tchaiko-chan!

10:16.070 --> 10:17.630
Wait, why me?

10:21.760 --> 10:23.080
School?

10:23.680 --> 10:26.140
Shoebill Academy Sports Festival

10:24.050 --> 10:26.140
Is this part of the Musik's power?

10:26.380 --> 10:30.230
The next event is the three-legged race.

10:30.430 --> 10:32.380
Three-legged race?

10:32.380 --> 10:33.450
Wait, what?

10:34.110 --> 10:35.110
What?

10:35.330 --> 10:36.220
Why?

10:36.220 --> 10:37.550
So many strangers...

10:37.550 --> 10:38.340
I'm scared.

10:38.340 --> 10:39.990
You're kind of annoying.

10:40.340 --> 10:42.080
Ready...

10:42.080 --> 10:43.870
Set...

10:43.870 --> 10:44.620
Go!

10:53.130 --> 10:55.510
Why is this kid on top of me?

10:55.510 --> 10:56.600
I just fell!

10:56.600 --> 10:57.650
Don't look at me!

10:57.650 --> 10:58.370
I'll fall in love.

10:58.370 --> 11:00.090
R-Right back at you.

11:00.460 --> 11:02.360
It's not like I like you or—

11:02.360 --> 11:03.300
What is this, a romcom?

11:03.560 --> 11:06.560
You're totally wrong if you think
I'll fall in love with you this easily!

11:08.610 --> 11:09.170
Huh?

11:13.840 --> 11:17.030
A puppy in the rain.

11:18.280 --> 11:19.690
You're so crafty!

11:25.340 --> 11:26.300
Stop it!

11:27.130 --> 11:28.200
Stop it!

11:28.200 --> 11:31.520
I'll fall in love with you
if I see you helping a puppy.

11:31.520 --> 11:33.130
I'll fall in love with you!

11:33.960 --> 11:34.910
But...

11:35.200 --> 11:36.220
Hey.

11:37.830 --> 11:38.910
Schu?

11:42.590 --> 11:45.310
Why don't you do something?

11:45.310 --> 11:46.680
Look at him. He's soaking.

11:47.340 --> 11:51.620
Is this one of those things where a wild guy
shows a softer side for animals?!

11:50.600 --> 11:54.190
A man's gotta help those in need.

11:51.620 --> 11:53.760
But why is he so into it?

11:54.370 --> 11:56.110
Sorry.

11:57.440 --> 11:58.440
It's all right.

11:58.440 --> 12:02.630
And now he's going to steal my heart
with the delinquent laugh!

12:02.630 --> 12:04.820
The Musik has you by the balls!

12:06.250 --> 12:07.870
Let's bounce.

12:08.220 --> 12:10.370
To your gaming room!

12:12.790 --> 12:13.960
Go!

12:18.450 --> 12:20.740
They're pairing off.

12:25.510 --> 12:27.430
That was close.

12:27.750 --> 12:28.580
Damn.

12:32.070 --> 12:34.480
Where's the soap?

12:34.480 --> 12:36.340
What are you doing?

12:36.340 --> 12:40.520
Like the evening calm, a
small room balances the mind,

12:40.520 --> 12:45.910
for it spares the eyes and
ears of the superfluous noise.

12:46.190 --> 12:48.330
This is more of a cabinet than a room.

12:49.860 --> 12:51.010
Do you have a fever?

12:51.010 --> 12:52.210
Don't look at me!

12:55.060 --> 12:56.010
Beethes-san?

13:21.210 --> 13:24.610
The Hasshies don't seem
to remember me at all.

13:25.030 --> 13:26.130
What can they do?

13:26.130 --> 13:28.000
It's all because of the Musik.

13:28.000 --> 13:28.690
Yup.

13:28.690 --> 13:29.930
It's your fault, Tchaiko-chan.

13:29.930 --> 13:32.490
Why do you need to do that every single time?

13:32.490 --> 13:33.750
It's true.

13:34.030 --> 13:35.950
Every single time!

13:34.580 --> 13:39.280
Hasshie's a bit too unhinged,
even with the Musik's influence.

13:35.950 --> 13:37.420
It's true!

13:37.420 --> 13:38.100
Shut up!

13:38.100 --> 13:39.990
Every single time!

13:39.280 --> 13:41.990
And people are pairing off way too easily.

13:41.990 --> 13:43.410
Something's not right.

13:44.600 --> 13:45.810
I've got it!

13:46.500 --> 13:48.570
Time's almost up.

13:48.570 --> 13:51.560
Hasshie's freaking out because
he falls asleep at night.

13:51.560 --> 13:55.810
I think the three of us can get out
if we hold off until the sun goes down.

13:56.420 --> 13:57.690
I see...

13:57.690 --> 13:59.610
I'm running out of time.

13:59.830 --> 14:02.760
We can survive, Tchaiko-chan!

14:03.510 --> 14:05.240
All right, then.

14:06.000 --> 14:08.670
We're going to the afterlife together!

14:08.670 --> 14:09.660
The afterlife?

14:09.660 --> 14:10.750
Why?

14:19.980 --> 14:22.420
Dude, is it really a time
to be watching ballet?

14:22.860 --> 14:25.050
This is Swan Lake.

14:25.340 --> 14:28.080
The prince encounters a lady named Odette,

14:28.080 --> 14:31.640
who had been transformed into
a swan, and pledges his love.

14:31.640 --> 14:35.280
Alas, deceived by the evil
sorcerer Von Rothbart,

14:35.280 --> 14:37.280
he becomes engaged to a false Odette.

14:37.280 --> 14:40.210
Betrayed, Odette takes her own life.

14:40.210 --> 14:43.300
That's the tragedy of Swan Lake.

14:43.300 --> 14:48.450
But there are versions with a happy ending
where the prince's love breaks the curse.

14:48.650 --> 14:52.030
Swan Lake is so feelsy.

14:52.030 --> 14:53.950
Good for you, Odette.

14:54.390 --> 14:57.990
If Swan Lake has a happy ending...

14:57.990 --> 15:03.210
Could this be not a Musik of love
and death, but of love and rebirth?

15:03.450 --> 15:04.570
That's it.

15:04.570 --> 15:08.120
Maybe once you pair off with someone,
you don't die, but you win the game.

15:08.120 --> 15:09.890
We're alive, right?

15:09.890 --> 15:12.570
Come on, I lost <i>all</i> my items.

15:12.570 --> 15:13.890
Wait a second.

15:14.210 --> 15:18.180
If you can get out once you
pair off, doesn't that mean...

15:18.180 --> 15:21.270
I'm the only one who can save Bąda-kyun!

15:21.720 --> 15:23.290
No, it doesn't have to be you, tool.

15:23.290 --> 15:24.880
I'll be back!

15:24.880 --> 15:26.210
Bąda-kyun!

15:26.970 --> 15:29.190
What does he think he's going to do?

15:29.520 --> 15:34.180
But if this really is a
Musik of love and rebirth,

15:34.180 --> 15:35.870
Tchaiko's feelings must be for...

15:47.360 --> 15:48.970
You don't even have more than one piece!

15:48.970 --> 15:50.380
I wrote more!

15:50.380 --> 15:51.560
No one's even heard of them!

15:51.060 --> 15:52.470
Those voices...

15:51.560 --> 15:52.840
Yes, they have!

15:52.840 --> 15:55.680
Sousuke, have you ever heard of
the suspension bridge effect?

15:55.680 --> 15:56.920
No, I haven't.

15:56.920 --> 15:58.180
Where did that come from?

15:58.180 --> 16:01.720
When two people cross a rocking
suspension ridge together,

16:01.720 --> 16:04.500
they can confuse the excitement with love.

16:04.500 --> 16:06.140
And they're more likely to hook up.

16:06.140 --> 16:07.420
Really?

16:12.240 --> 16:14.950
Bąda-chan, Tchaiko-chan, stop it, please!

16:15.240 --> 16:18.330
You were bent on snuffing
me out from the beginning.

16:18.330 --> 16:21.750
As if! I would have it a lot easier if I
could use my Musik the way I wanted to.

16:21.750 --> 16:23.240
I hate you!

16:23.240 --> 16:26.120
I would have had a solo album
if you weren't around.

16:26.120 --> 16:29.170
Bach-sama would never have
let me go if it were just me.

16:31.070 --> 16:31.840
Look out!

16:33.670 --> 16:34.900
We aren't done

16:34.900 --> 16:36.850
talking yet!

16:39.280 --> 16:40.630
All right, let's continue.

16:40.630 --> 16:42.230
Bring it on!

16:42.580 --> 16:44.790
Th-Thank goodness.

16:46.700 --> 16:48.020
This is so exciting.

16:48.020 --> 16:49.280
Sousuke?!

16:49.280 --> 16:51.150
Bąda-chan!

16:51.530 --> 16:53.260
Bąda-chan, I'm here for you.

16:53.260 --> 16:54.240
So hook up with me.

16:54.240 --> 16:55.210
Go away!

17:05.330 --> 17:06.710
Tickle, tickle, tickle!

17:11.630 --> 17:14.160
Those damn birds aren't going to get me.

17:14.160 --> 17:17.670
I'm sending you to the
bottom with my bare hands.

17:17.670 --> 17:19.640
I dare you to try.

17:20.100 --> 17:20.990
Wait.

17:21.800 --> 17:24.940
We can get out of here if we pair off.

17:24.940 --> 17:26.850
So please, go out with me.

17:27.840 --> 17:30.040
I thought you died if you pair off.

17:30.040 --> 17:31.170
You don't.

17:31.170 --> 17:32.730
You win.

17:32.730 --> 17:35.070
This is a Musik of love and rebirth.

17:35.470 --> 17:37.970
Of love and rebirth?

17:38.780 --> 17:40.770
I don't know anything about it.

17:40.770 --> 17:42.070
It's true.

17:42.070 --> 17:44.540
Everyone else is totally fine.
They're waiting outside.

17:45.330 --> 17:48.480
Were you trying to reboot Claskey Klasky?

17:48.480 --> 17:51.000
Is that what you really want?

17:51.260 --> 17:54.550
D-Don't get the wrong idea!

17:57.100 --> 17:58.760
Then...

17:59.170 --> 18:02.080
Then why don't you take me on properly?

18:02.610 --> 18:06.430
You've been acting weird
ever since I used my Musik.

18:06.430 --> 18:07.490
Me?

18:08.150 --> 18:11.720
I guess I got a bit big-headed, too.

18:11.720 --> 18:15.790
But that was because I was proud that
I was finally up to par with you.

18:17.580 --> 18:21.410
You thought you were inferior to me?

18:22.010 --> 18:23.580
But not anymore.

18:24.000 --> 18:25.840
We can climb up together.

18:26.690 --> 18:30.780
You're the only one fit for me.

18:30.780 --> 18:33.160
I'm sure that man thinks so, too.

18:33.700 --> 18:36.970
B-Bądarzews—

18:37.880 --> 18:40.090
I-It's huge!

18:51.650 --> 18:54.560
You're the one for me.

18:54.560 --> 18:55.570
I know.

18:56.120 --> 18:58.960
You aren't going to leave me behind?

18:58.960 --> 19:02.030
I could never leave you
behind if you got serious.

19:08.710 --> 19:09.970
Wait up!

19:09.970 --> 19:11.510
Bąda-kyun's supposed to pair up with me!

19:11.510 --> 19:12.640
Here we go!

19:19.180 --> 19:21.200
A couple is born.

19:21.200 --> 19:22.180
Yup.

19:27.120 --> 19:28.570
Wait, huh?

19:29.480 --> 19:32.490
I'm left behind?

19:39.400 --> 19:41.260
B-Beethes.

19:43.420 --> 19:45.200
I can't hold on for long.

19:45.200 --> 19:47.620
I don't know what to do.

19:48.960 --> 19:51.370
This is a Musik of love and rebirth.

19:51.950 --> 19:52.880
I know.

19:53.110 --> 19:56.280
We can get out of here if we pair off.

19:57.970 --> 19:59.110
What's wrong, Beethes?

20:00.840 --> 20:03.040
Th-This situation...

20:03.040 --> 20:04.100
Nay.

20:04.100 --> 20:08.310
Pay no heed to the mischievous
impulses of desire.

20:09.930 --> 20:13.150
You're pretty manly today.

20:27.200 --> 20:28.450
What are you doing?

20:28.870 --> 20:32.000
Oh, uh, is everyone safe?

20:32.360 --> 20:35.310
Tchaiko and Bąda went home hand-in-hand.

20:35.720 --> 20:38.000
The Musik is over.

20:42.040 --> 20:46.150
Very few relationships begun in the
heat of the moment are lasting.

20:46.150 --> 20:47.330
Relationships?!

20:47.330 --> 20:49.500
It's all right, Kanae.

20:49.500 --> 20:52.160
I'm not the type who cares
about a girl's past.

20:52.160 --> 20:53.810
I have no past!

20:53.810 --> 20:56.770
Look, he's frozen.

20:56.770 --> 20:58.680
Let me go!

20:59.020 --> 21:00.020
He jerked.

21:00.020 --> 21:01.690
I do not approve!

21:01.690 --> 21:04.100
How could you become a couple with Senpai?!

21:04.100 --> 21:05.990
There is no couple!

21:06.230 --> 21:08.070
Music...

21:10.550 --> 21:16.250
Yes, this was all in service of music!

21:16.430 --> 21:19.700
All passions of the loin are but
adventures for the artist's soul!

21:19.700 --> 21:20.900
Okay, okay.

21:20.170 --> 21:23.320
Explorations of the flesh are
carried out with deepest intent.

21:20.900 --> 21:21.860
Good for you.

21:21.860 --> 21:23.020
Not good.

21:23.020 --> 21:24.340
I don't even get it.

21:23.320 --> 21:26.260
Only by burning onto the mind's eye
the new scenery that comes with it

21:26.260 --> 21:30.790
can there be purpose enough to
overcome the shame, the humiliation,

21:30.790 --> 21:33.740
the masochism inherent
to the human condition...

21:35.330 --> 21:37.980
Thank you, everyone.

21:41.220 --> 21:43.870
Tchaiko-chan, your position.

21:44.780 --> 21:46.090
You're too far back.

21:46.090 --> 21:48.320
My face is going to look huge.

21:49.050 --> 21:50.790
Now you're too far out.

21:50.790 --> 21:52.810
Don't cut into my spotlight.

21:55.580 --> 21:58.130
You can go home, Tchaiko-chan...

21:59.460 --> 22:02.180
What's with the attitude?!

22:02.180 --> 22:03.680
We're breaking up!

22:03.680 --> 22:06.270
You're fired if you say
we're breaking up, you know.

22:06.270 --> 22:08.110
Break... Break...

22:08.110 --> 22:09.820
We're a breakout!

22:09.820 --> 22:11.200
Breakout, huh?

22:11.200 --> 22:12.720
Breaking out what?

22:12.720 --> 22:13.650
Breaking out of prison?

22:13.650 --> 22:15.580
Are you going to run away?

22:15.860 --> 22:19.770
Then I'll b... b... babby!

22:19.770 --> 22:21.210
Get her, Bąda-kyun!

22:21.210 --> 22:22.650
Hang in there, Tchaiko!

22:22.650 --> 22:25.220
Is Mommy staying up all
night to knit you a mitten?

22:25.220 --> 22:26.610
They're super popular.

22:26.610 --> 22:29.410
It looks like they'll last a little longer.

22:29.410 --> 22:31.160
Great thinking, Bach-sama.

22:43.000 --> 22:46.010
To be continued

22:43.800 --> 22:44.750
Huh?

24:15.970 --> 24:25.940
Mozart is the Name

24:16.790 --> 24:19.310
There's nothing to do
in this world but laugh.

24:19.310 --> 24:20.560
Do not seek meaning.

24:20.560 --> 24:22.630
Things simply exist.

24:22.630 --> 24:23.880
The sunset calls out.

24:23.880 --> 24:25.790
All things are just.

24:25.790 --> 24:29.400
They have always been
and always will be.
